    \ingroup vscodeext-how-to-csharp

    \title Build and run Qt Bridge for C# applications

    A \l {Qt Bridge for C#} project is a regular .NET project. Build and run it
    with the .NET command-line tools or with C# Dev Kit.

    Before you build, make sure that the build finds a Qt installation. For
    more information, see
    \l {vscodeext-how-to-select-qt-csharp.html}
    {Select Qt for Qt Bridge for C# projects}.

    The first build takes longer, because it also generates and builds the
    native code that connects C# and QML.

    \section1 Build in the terminal

    To build and run the application, enter the following commands in the
    \uicontrol Terminal view:

    \code [text]
    dotnet build
    dotnet run
    \endcode

    To build a particular configuration, add \c {-c}, for example
    \c {dotnet build -c Release}.

    \section1 Build with C# Dev Kit

    If you installed the C# Dev Kit extension, you can also build the project
    from the \uicontrol {Solution Explorer} view: right-click the project, and
    select \uicontrol Build. To run or debug the application with the C#
    debugger, right-click the project, and select \uicontrol Debug.

    C# Dev Kit builds the project outside the \uicontrol Terminal view, so it
    does not get the \uicontrol {Qt Dir} setting. On Windows ARM64, Linux, and
    macOS, set the \c QtDir environment variable before you start VS Code, or
    set \c QtDir in the project.

    \section1 Debug the application

    To debug the QML code of the application with the QML debugger, or the C#
    code with C# Dev Kit, see
    \l {vscodeext-how-debug-apps-csharp.html}
    {Debug Qt Bridge for C# applications}.

    \section1 Use the QML tools after the build

    The build generates metadata that the QML language server, QML Preview,
    and \QP need for your C# types and QML modules. After the first build,
    the code completion in QML files knows the types that you expose from C#.

    If you build the project in several configurations or for several target
    frameworks, select the build that the QML tools should use. For more
    information, see
    \l {vscodeext-how-to-preview-csharp.html}
    {Preview and profile Qt Bridge for C# applications}.

    \sa {vscodeext-tutorials-qt-csharp.html}{Tutorial: Qt Bridge for C#}
*/
